 { White has a power outpost on c5. Fortunately for Black, they are in time to undermine it. Can you see how? } 21... { -KEY- } a5 $1 { Correct! Black gets rid of their isolated pawn at the same time as they soften up the defense of the knight on c5. } ( 21... Rfe8 $2 { Black would be unwise to waste time. Here, White could stop Black's a-pawn advance by playing: } 22. Ra1 $1 { Suddenly, Black has not only lost their ability to break down White's power outpost. They also have to contend with managing the weakness of the a6 pawn. } Ra8 { The attempt to renew the threat of playing ... a5 does not work here, as White can put a stop to it with their next move. } 23. Ra5 $16 { Black will struggle to defend the position due to the chronically weak pawn on a6. } ) 
22. Rb1 axb4 $1 23. cxb4 $11 { White has kept their power outpost for now, but the damage to their structure ensures that Black is at least equal. } 
