 { Black wants to reach the outpost on f4, but right now there is no possible maneuver. Can you find the sequence that will help Black to bring a piece to this square? Black to play. } 18... { -KEY- } gxh5 $1 19. gxh5 ( 19. Bxg5 $2 { stops Black's plan, but the loss of the dark-squared bishop is too high a price to pay. After } hxg5 20. gxh5 Bh6 $17 { Black will be able to break with ...g4 soon, when the White king will be in a lot of trouble due to the weakness of the dark squares. } ) 
Nh3 $17 { Correct! Black is now ready to step the knight to f4 on the next move. Note that after a sequence of moves like Be2-f1 ...Nf4 Bxf4 exf4 Black does not mind their damaged pawn structure since now their dark-squared bishop springs to life along the a1-h8 diagonal. } 
