 { White has several ways of converting their winning position. One of these is to play f4-f5, creating an outpost on f4 and following this up by playing Ne2-f4. However, there is an even more forcing way of reaching an advanced outpost, by using tactics and calculation. White to play. } 31. { -KEY- } Nh5 $3 { The knight is headed to the f6 square, from where it will rip apart Black's kingside defenses. } Rh8 { Pinning the knight is Black's best try, but now White shows their idea in full. } ( 31... gxh5 { Black cannot save themselves by grabbing the knight. } 32. Qxh5 Rg6 { If ...Kg7 then Qh7 is mate. } 33. Qh7 Rg7 34. Qxg7 Kxg7 35. Rh7 Kg8 36. Rxe7 $18 { with an easily winning endgame. } ) 
32. Nf6 $3 { Sacrificing the queen! } Rxh4 33. Rxh4 $18 ( { Correct! Black is helpless against the threat of mate on h7. The best try is } 33. Rxh4 Qxf6 { but after } 34. gxf6 { White will be an exchange to the good. } ) 

